1050: operator. At I12 the construction uses the actual multiplicative
1051: unit charts: choose a frame on the first rational component and
1052: continue across the successive node units eta_i. The continued
1053: frame on the last component agrees with the first because
1054: product eta_i=1. The units and their logarithms extend smoothly in Q,
1055: so this normalized frame extends over the nodal charts. Two such
1056: normalized local frames differ by a function of the base alone,
1057: because a holomorphic function on a connected compact fibre is
1058: constant. Their transition functions define a line bundle on C.
1059: This proves, for the actual transported line, the equality
1060: 
1061:     c1(L)=c1(O(P'-O'))+n F       for an integer n.
1062: 
1063: It proves the required filtration statement via explicit normalized
1064: frames. In particular it does not infer that equality merely from
1065: triviality of the action on the associated graded of Leray.
1066: Since F²=F.(P'-O')=0, its square is exactly-2. The smooth affine
1067: comparison preserves orientation and signature, so p1 of the compact
1068: sheet pairs to-24. The unspecified integer n records the permitted
1069: boundary gauge and has no effect on either of these pairings.
1070: 
1071: ## P3F.13. Exact angular clutch at the parameter corner
1072: 
1073: For the default twists let F(s,v) be the exact origin difference in
1074: P2.2, and keep gamma(s,v)=(6mu,C-s-12v). Direct polynomial subtraction
1075: gives, for real theta,
1076: 
1077:     F(s,v+theta)-F(s,v)
1078:        = theta gamma(s,v)+6theta(1-theta)delta.       (P3F.13.1)
1079: 
1080: On a fixed-radius parameter circle, v=ib+theta. The final summand is
1081: real in the delta direction. It is a unitary gauge, equal to1 after
1082: exponentiation at both endpoints. It can be removed by a homotopy
1083: of periodic gauges. The circle quotient of the origin comparison is
1084: therefore exactly the gamma-translation loop, with all radial terms
1085: independent of theta.
1086: 
1087: The base deck must still be retained. Since gamma(s+12,v)=
1088: gamma(s,v)-12delta,
1089: 
1090:     [F(s+12,v+theta)-F(s+12,v)]
1091:        -[F(s,v+theta)-F(s,v)]=-12theta delta.        (P3F.13.2)
1092: 
1093: Thus the two angular lifts differ on the Q deck by the unitary gauge
1094: exp(-24pi i theta) in the exp(2pi i zeta2) convention, of winding-12.
1095: This gauge is the integral clutch of the circle line. It does not
1096: disappear on passing to the orbit: its degree is retained by the
1097: principal circle bundle. compact_torsor.py checks both exact
1098: identities and the endpoint values.
1099: 
1100: The normal-crossing chart suggested by the second Tate multiplier is
1101: XY=Qr after q=Q^12, because q r^12=(Qr)^12. Its elementary small
1102: resolution has charts
1103: 
1104:     X=Qz, r=zY;          Q=Xw, Y=wr.
1105: 
1106: At a node Q=uv of the resolved source I12 surface the remaining
1107: chart uv=Xw is resolved by
1108: 
1109:     X=uk, v=kw;          u=Xk, w=kv.
1110: 
1111: These four-variable charts are smooth and separate the central fixed
1112: surface from the fixed cusp trace. They give the local candidate for
1113: an orbit bordism after deleting fixed tubes. The central fixed-sheet
1114: normals have opposite weights and product trivial, so their positive
1115: Hopf projectivization is a product S2 bundle with Euler class
1116: u+c1(L). This inner boundary is nonspin when the compact sheet has
1117: K=5F. The canonical quotient structure is spin^c with determinant
1118: -K on that boundary; no claim that this compact product is spin is
1119: made.
1120: 
1121: Historical scope of this complex corner attempt: its cyclic descent
1122: and outer identification after resolving the source I12 charts were
1123: not completed. P3F.13 proves the exact local clutch, including its
1124: line gauge. The actual global application is now proved by the real
1125: trace P3K.6--7, the analytic symbol comparison P3K.8, and the rotating
1126: normal framing P3K.9. Those constructions retain the same clutch and
1127: compute the original return without asserting this complex corner
1128: completion.
1129: 
1130: ## P3F.14. Proved: the characteristic formula for an actual fixed-sheet boundary
1131: 
1132: This is the general calculation for the explicitly specified Hopf
1133: boundary. The earlier complex corner attempt did not supply a global
1134: boundary identification; the actual real trace P3K.6--9 now supplies
1135: the application and its complete orientation and line comparison. Let S be a compact
1136: complex surface, and let L_+,L_- be its two complex normal lines of
1137: circle weights+1,-1 in a stable complex eight-dimensional chart.
1138: Write a=c1(L_+), b=c1(L_-), d=c1(TS). Its free normal-sphere quotient
1139: is B=P(L_+ direct-sum conjugate(L_-)). Orient its sphere fibre so that
1140: the circle Euler class x has integral1. Then
1141: 
1142:     pi_*(x)=1, pi_*(x²)=a-b,
1143:     pi_*(x³)=a²-ab+b²,
1144:     p1(TB)=pi^*(p1(TS)+(a+b)²).
1145: 
1146: These follow from the projective-bundle relation with roots a,-b.
1147: The stable complex structure inherited from the original two opposite
1148: weights has spin^c determinant D=pi^*(d+a+b). Indeed the associated
1149: normal lines have opposite circle characters, so those characters
1150: cancel in their determinant. The degree-six spin^c index polynomial
1151: for this structure twisted by the circle line is
1152: 
1153:     integral_B exp(D/2) exp(x) Ahat(TB).
1154: 
1155: Substitution of the four displayed pushforwards gives exactly
1156: 
1157:     (3d²-p1(TS))/24 + (a²+ad)/2
1158:        = chi(O_S)+(a²-a.K_S)/2
1159:        = chi(S,L_+).
1160: 
1161: The equality on the right is the surface Riemann--Roch polynomial;
1162: the calculation also proves that the negative-weight normal line b
1163: cancels entirely. No spin structure on S or on B is required.
1164: For an actual spin-six boundary with D=0 the same index polynomial is
1165: (4x³-p1 x)/24, the integer A used in P3F.11.
1166: 
1167: For the compact fixed sheet of P3F.12, a=M+nF, chi(O)=1,
1168: M²=-2, M.K=F²=M.F=0. Its index contribution is therefore0 for every
1169: such fibre-supported shift. The fixed cusp curve has positive normal
1170: line O(-1); its Dolbeault cohomology on P1 is zero in both degrees.
1171: These are exact local index inputs. P3K.6--8 subsequently constructs
1172: the actual real bordism and identifies its spin-c symbol. The
1173: resulting return index therefore follows through that comparison;
1174: no analytic corner completion is asserted.
1175: 
1176: ## P3F.15. Proved: cyclic label and line-clutch identities
1177: 
1178: Here is the explicit descent on the rank-one node charts. Bounded
1179: nonzero period units are harmless in these identities: choose their
1180: logarithms on the cusp disc and split their twelfth roots in the
1181: following multipliers. Put rho=Qr, zeta=exp(2pi i/12), eta=exp(pi i/12),
1182: and index the node charts by i in Z, modulo the gamma period of length12:
1183: 
1184:     X_i=W/rho^i, Y_i=rho^(i+1)/W, X_i Y_i=rho.
1185: 
1186: The deck map on the dense torus is
1187: 
1188:     D:(Q,i,W)->(zeta Q,i-1,eta rho^(-1) W).
1189: 
1190: Consequently its formulas in the node charts are
1191: 
1192:     X'_(i-1)=eta zeta^(1-i) X_i,
1193:     Y'_(i-1)=eta^(-1) zeta^i Y_i.
1194: 
1195: Their product is zeta rho, as required for the new parameter. Both
1196: multipliers are units, so this map extends across each node and
1197: preserves the opposite circle weights. It is free on the twelve node
1198: labels even at Q=0. After twelve iterations the W multiplier is
1199: eta^12 zeta^(-66) rho^(-12)=rho^(-12), since the two first factors
1200: both equal-1. Accompany each step by the locally defined elliptic
1201: translation-P/2; the twelfth step is-6P. Thus the twelfth iterate is
1202: the inverse gamma period, including its source-translation part.
1203: This proves descent on the labelled rank-one charts.
1204: 
1205: On a fixed-radius r-circle, each factor rho^(-1) has angular winding-1.
1206: The twelve-step gauge has winding-12. It is exactly the winding in
1207: (P3F.13.2), with the same W/exp(zeta2) sign conversion. This verifies
1208: the integral circle-line clutch, not just the orbit action. It leaves the
1209: outer contraction in the earlier complex corner attempt unproved.
1210: The actual monodromy application is instead completed by the real
1211: trace P3K.6--9.
1212: 
1213: 
1214: Multiplicity check on the outstanding outer identification: a free
1215: action on the twelve labels, with reduced divisor Q=0 on those charts,
1216: would descend q=Q^12 to a divisor of multiplicity twelve. The actual
1217: outer cusp for r nonzero has multiplicity one. Thus the labelled
1218: fixed-sheet descent above cannot itself be its outer chart. A valid
1219: comparison must explicitly account for the ramification or fixed
1220: strata, or for a changed divisor multiplicity. The missing morphism
1221: is therefore stronger than merely contracting the additional source
1222: I12 exceptional curves.
